---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import foto from '../../assets/maria-denisse-biblioteca.png';
---
<Base lang="en" titulo="About" descripcion="Biography of María Denisse Fanianos de Capriles: journalist, columnist for El Universal and ACI Prensa, author and co-founder of Fundación Entre Líneas.">
  <section class="seccion">
    <div class="contenedor bio-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="etiqueta">Biography</p>
        <h1>About María Denisse</h1>
        <hr class="linea" />
        <div class="texto">
          <p class="intro">
            María Denisse Fanianos de Capriles is a Venezuelan journalist, writer, editor and opinion columnist.
            And, above all, a wife and the mother of six children.
          </p>
          <p>
            She was born in Caracas. In 1989 she graduated first in her class from the School of Social Communication at the
            Central University of Venezuela (UCV). Her thesis, <em lang="es">«¡Qué caricatura de democracia!»</em>
            (“What a caricature of democracy!”), received a distinction for excellence and was published. At the UCV she
            took part in research with professors Marcelino Bisbal, Adolfo Herrera, Gloria Cuenca and Eleazar Díaz Rangel.
          </p>

          <h2>Opinion columnist</h2>
          <p>
            From January 2011 she wrote a weekly column for the Caracas newspaper <em>El Universal</em>, covering social,
            civic, educational and family life in Venezuela. She published more than 200 articles there. Her column was
            dropped, along with those of some thirty other columnists, after the paper changed owners and editorial line.
          </p>
          <p>
            Her pieces were republished and covered by international outlets and agencies such as ACI Prensa, ACI Digital
            and El Observador de la Actualidad. She later went on writing from Venezuela as a columnist and reporter for
            ACI Prensa.
          </p>

          <h2>Author</h2>
          <p>
            In December 2019 she published her first book, <a href="/libro" lang="es"><em>¿Se puede ser feliz en Venezuela?</em></a>,
            a collection of her columns. It is now also available in English as
            <a href="/en/book"><em>Can You Be Happy in Venezuela?</em></a> At the publishing house she runs with her husband,
            the publisher Luis Felipe Capriles, she has worked as an author, compiler and copy editor.
          </p>

          <h2>Fundación Entre Líneas</h2>
          <p>
            In 1994 she founded, together with her husband, <a href="/en/foundation">Fundación Entre Líneas</a>, devoted to
            producing printed educational material for Venezuelans. She directed and produced the monthly bulletin
            <a href="https://venezuelaentrelineas.com/leer-entrelineas/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Leer Entre Líneas</em></a>,
            which was distributed free of charge across almost the whole country for years.
          </p>
          <p>
            In 2004 she organized, with nearly a hundred volunteers, the gathering “Builders of the New Participatory
            Venezuela”, with more than 40 organizations and 600 participants from every social, political and religious background.
          </p>

          <h2>Interviews</h2>
          <p>
            Over her career she has interviewed, among others, former president Luis Herrera Campins, the poet Ida Gramcko,
            Brother Ginés, Cardinal Jorge Urosa Savino, the apostolic nuncio Giacinto Berloco and Bishop Javier Echevarría.
          </p>

          <h2>In the media</h2>
          <p>
            Her columns and views have been featured by ACI Prensa, Aleteia and other outlets.
            <a href="/en/press">See all press coverage →</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <Image src={foto} alt="María Denisse Fanianos de Capriles" widths={[320, 480, 640]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 80vw, 340px" class="foto" />
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .bio-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
  .texto { max-width: 680px; }
  .texto h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; margin-top: 1.6em; }
  .foto { border-radius: 4px; position: sticky; top: 24px; box-shadow: 0 18px 40px -20px rgba(29,42,71,.45); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .bio-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    aside { order: -1; max-width: 300px; }
    .foto { position: static; }
  }
</style>
